course: dictionary
lesson: 8582
title: Science has three meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: The word science can mean three things, and context tells you which one. First, it means finding out how the world works by watching carefully, asking questions, testing ideas and measuring.
explain: Second, it is a school subject that studies living things, materials, forces, the Earth and space. In «Our science lesson today is about magnets», the word means the school subject.
explain: Third, it is a branch of knowledge, such as physics, chemistry or biology. Phrases like «science fair», «science project» and «science fiction» are fixed phrases: read the whole phrase to understand it.
explain: To choose the right meaning, read the words around science. In «Scientists change their ideas when new evidence appears», science means the way people find things out, not a school subject.
fact: Science means finding out how the world works by watching, asking questions, testing ideas and measuring.
fact: A fair test changes only one thing at a time, so the results tell you something true.
fact: «Swallows migrate to warm Africa every autumn and come back in spring» because in a British winter there are almost no flying insects to eat. This is true science.
fact: Scientists change their ideas when new evidence appears.
fact: «Science fiction» is a type of story that imagines future or impossible science.
exercise: In «Our science lesson today is about magnets», what does science mean? | A sports game | *A school subject that studies forces and materials | A type of fizzy drink | A kind of cooking
exercise: «Scientists change their ideas when new evidence appears.» What does this tell you about science? | Evidence is a type of sweet | *Ideas can change when new evidence is found | Science is only about old ideas | Scientists never change their minds
exercise: In «science fiction», what does the word science point to? | Cheering at a football match | *Imagined future or impossible science | Cooking in a kitchen | Learning a new language
test: «Swallows feed on flying insects, and in a British winter there are almost none, so swallows migrate.» Why do swallows migrate? | *Because there are almost no flying insects to eat in a British winter | Because they want to see the snow | Because they like the sun in Britain | Because the sea is too cold for them
test: Which of these is a branch of science? | *Physics | Lunch | Football | Fiction
exam: In «the science project» in the story about two classmates racing to finish first, what kind of thing is a science project? | A game of tag | A type of lunch | *A piece of school work about finding things out | A music lesson on drums
